  "correct": "E",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Sketch the two curves together",
      "body": "<p>Sketch the cubic and the straight line on the same axes. Compare a positive, zero and negative line gradient.</p>",
      "recap": "Intersections and the curve order determine an enclosed area.",
      "pitfall": "Do not divide by x before checking x=0.",
      "pause": "Set the two heights equal and factor to find the intersections.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Intersections and the curve order determine an enclosed area."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the symmetry to reduce the work",
      "body": "<p>Compare both curves at x and −x. If the enclosed regions have equal areas, calculate one and account for the other.</p>",
      "recap": "Geometric areas are positive even when their signed integrals cancel.",
      "pitfall": "Integrating straight through both sides can hide the total area.",
      "pause": "Set up an upper-minus-lower integral for one region.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Geometric areas are positive even when their signed integrals cancel."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Evaluate before finding m",
      "body": "<p>Integrate with m held constant. Substitute the limits you found, then form the total area and equate it to the given value.</p>",
      "recap": "The given area applies to the entire enclosed region.",
      "pitfall": "Keep only a parameter value compatible with your intersection sketch.",
      "pause": "Solve for m and check the total area.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l20",
          "reminder": "Integrate each power and substitute both limits."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>The intersections are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x000B1;</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. On <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, mx lies above <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. The two enclosed regions are equal by symmetry.</p><p>The total area is 2<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"integral from 0 to the square root of m of (m x minus x cubed), with respect to x\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.18em\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> = 2<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" aria-label=\"m x squared over 2 minus x to the fourth over 4, evaluated from 0 to the square root of m\"><msubsup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>0</mn><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></msubsup></math> = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer E: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>.</strong></p>",
